    },
    "body": "Absent-owner stop requests can copy another owner's fact because an existing recent-source transform rewards position 10. Unrelated six-word filler reproduces the same error. A bounded Rust fitter neutralizes that one learned transform while preserving the entire remaining parent model and its exact source identities. The new witness reconstructs parent 91ede422; a matched control restores its source router.\n\nRetain 82662f85 at this bounded scope. Actual generation improves 40/40 versus 32/40 under the parent-router control; original abstention improves 10/10 versus 6/10. Post-selection fixed-form transfer passes 32/32 versus 20/32, with no retuning. All 663 retained answers, 132 word construction, 28 word open, 24 earlier transfer cases, 14 historical semantic reports and 12 full history identities are preserved. Native API passes 166/166; 29 focused tests include the kernel source guard and six actual-artifact allocation/checkpoint checks. 24 generated Rust equalities and four identifier-return fragments compile and execute.\n\nThe new writer trace independently finds an exact 21-key instruction/fact proposal collision. That writer limitation remains unchanged and determines the next representation step. Original owner-first composition and two response-length overflow failures remain outside this correction. General prose, reasoning, synthesis, alpha and energy advantage are unqualified; new-artifact browser/WASM/HTTP and the blanket full suite were not run.\n\nThe result and evidence record bind the artifact, source, actual commands, retained controls, negative results and cumulative resources. Source review found no answer rule, parser, new decoder, matrix-product serving or provider path. Final formatting and claim checks are recorded locally; required PR/queue status names are compatibility acknowledgements that execute no tests.\n\nReferences #973.\n",
